    The VGA.COM utility offers the following functions:

    VGA FONT <file>       load character font (see FONTMAN.DOC)
                          depending on the size of the font file
                          the screen mode will be changed to
                          25/28/33/40/50 text lines

    VGA PAL <file>        load color palette (see PALMAN.DOC)
                          Option /F   to make palette reset resistant
                                 /R   to deactivate /F option

    VGA LINES 25|28|50    select 25/28/50 line mode by activating
                          one of the built-in standard character fonts

    VGA FRAME <color>     select frame ("overscan") color

    VGA BLINK | BRIGHT    toggle blink attribute / bright background

    VGA GREY | COLOR      select gray scale/color mode (incl. VGA reset)

    VGA RESET             Reset (current video mode)


    Instructions may be combined, for example:

        VGA grey, font SANSERIF.FNT
        VGA font SANSERIF.FNT, pal MY.PAL, bright, frame yellow

    An equal sign may preceed the specification:

        VGA font=SANSERIF.FNT, frame=yellow

